A split projective arrangement is a finite set of codimension-one linear subspaces of a vector space of dimension $`n+1`, regarded as hyperplanes in its projectivization.
For $`H_0\in\mathcal{P}` with equation $`\ell_0`, the slice $`\ell_0=1` is an affine $`n`-space, and intersecting the other hyperplanes with it gives the decone arrangement.

The slice depends on $`\ell_0` and not only on $`H_0`, so in the formalization the decone is indexed by $`\ell_0`.
The blueprint leaves the ring of $`U_{\mathcal{P}}` implicit, and the declarations of this box include it.
