The projective Betti polynomial is the decone polynomial and satisfies $`P_{c\mathcal{P}}(t)=(1+t)P_{\mathcal{P}}(t)`.
In particular $`b_1(U_{\mathcal{P}})=|\mathcal{P}|-1`.

Here $`b_q` is the polynomial coefficient, and the declarations include the module statements above, which require choices and carry the caveat about the zero ring.
